  "slug": "rocket-city-furmeet",
  "name": "Rocket City FurMeet",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Rocket City FurMeet (RCFM) was an annual furry convention in Huntsville, Alabama, held over Memorial Day weekend from 2003 to 2012. It was started by Brody Catsmouth, KO and members of North Alabama Regional Furs, and run by Rocket City FurMeet, Incorporated, a 501(c)(7) social club. The name refers to Huntsville's nickname, Rocket City, for the Redstone Arsenal and the US Space and Rocket Center. It was held at the Radisson Suite Hotel, later the Embassy Suites and the Hilton Garden Inn, and was known for its many food events and its \"Wheel of Blame\", spun at the opening and closing ceremonies. Its charity was Parenting Children of a Different Species, and attendance grew from 103 to over 350.",
